.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-POWER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-power
.Nd battery, AC, CPU frequency and suspend
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | suspend | governors | idle
.Nm
.Cm event Cm lid | Cm button
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Bl -tag -width "event lid|button"
.It Cm status
Battery, AC, the current CPU frequency governor, and temperature.
.It Cm suspend
Suspend to RAM, using deep sleep or s2idle, whichever the firmware
offers.
.It Cm governors
List the CPU frequency governors this kernel has.
.It Cm idle
What the compositor is doing about idling, and which clients, if any,
are holding the machine awake.
.It Cm event Cm lid | Cm button
Act on a hardware event.
Called by
acpid(8)
from
.Pa /etc/acpi/ ;
not normally run by a person.
.El
.Pp
Policy is declared state rather than a command here:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-state set power.governor powersave
# novi-state set power.lid      ignore
# novi-state set power.button   suspend
# novi-state apply
.Ed
.Ss Locking before sleep
A lid-close suspend locks the session first when
.Va power.lid.lock
is on, waiting about six seconds for the lock screen to appear and
then sleeping regardless: a closed lid is a machine in a bag, and
refusing to sleep trades a shoulder-surfing risk for a thermal one.
An
.Em idle
suspend is the opposite call.
.Va power.suspend.lock
is on by default and the machine does
.Em not
suspend if the lock screen fails to appear, because a machine left
awake is recoverable by anyone who walks up to it and one that
suspended unlocked is not.
.Pp
A machine with no root password therefore never idle-suspends with the
lock on:
novi-lockscreen(1)
refuses to run without a password.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/run/novi/display" -compact
.It Pa /run/novi/display
Published by the compositor so that a tool started from
acpid(8)
can find the Wayland session.
Absent means there is nothing to lock.
.It Pa /etc/acpi/PWRF/00000080
.It Pa /etc/acpi/LID/00000080
Named by busybox
acpid(8) Ns 's
compiled-in table, not by Novi.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0013 and RFC 0035.
.Sh CAVEATS
No suspend or resume on this system has been verified on physical
hardware.
